From 125cd184078d872c04c740b3266e4004c5dff6af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MATIAS <mnpn31@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:59:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Added view for the `Kundt Tube` experiment

Six touches, same shape as the existing experiments: three route constants, the
API client, the type module, the loader, the page and one line in the router.
Purely additive: no existing file loses a line and no shared component changes.

Beyond the plain controls the page shows the amplitude against plunger
position, which is the experiment itself; a clipping detector, since mic_peak
past 31000 means the analog front end is saturating and the amplitude is no
longer trustworthy; a headroom warning below x4, because amplitude multiplies
at resonance and a level set outside one will clip every peak; the
amplitude/RMS ratio, which separates measuring the tone from measuring room
noise; and the speed of sound from the spacing between maxima, v = 2 * d * f.

Two things worth knowing when reviewing:

The sweep curve only records a point when position and amplitude are both
present. The microphone and plunger modules publish independently, and an
amplitude without the position it was taken at is not a measurement. With no
plunger module connected the chart stays empty, which is correct.

The audio is a reconstruction and is labelled as such in the UI: an
OscillatorNode at the commanded frequency whose gain follows the Goertzel
magnitude. The microphone sends scalars, never waveforms.
